BRO-LMPC derives from TWIT_LMPC by Zirui Zang (zzangupenn),
https://github.com/zzangupenn/TWIT_LMPC . The source Apache-2.0 LICENSE is retained.
Source revision, working-file fingerprints, and local dependency fingerprints
are recorded in docs/source_manifest.json.

Adapted material includes dynamic-ST/kinematic fallback equations, trajectory
reference interpolation, track/spline/raceline utilities, conditional flow
bijectors, the neural spline flow, and the retained GPJax research classes.
New orchestration, configuration, planner kernels, value-training lifecycle,
checkpoint/data formats, diagnostics, tests, and benchmarks are in BRO-LMPC.

The original flow code identifies Distrax (Google DeepMind) as its reference.
F1TENTH remains a separately installed dependency with its own license notices.
Packaged track assets are copied from the source repository for compatibility.
